{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531130-v20-and-earlied-angellis-ater-what-path-road","id":1531130,"title":"[V20 and earlied] Angellis Ater what Path/Road ...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-19T11:14:45-08:00","id":1531130,"title":"[V20 and earlied] Angellis Ater what Path/Road ...","content":"I'm a bit confused by the Angellis Ater and what actually their deal is since the different sources are pretty contradictory.<br /> <br /> I'm mean there is obviously a connection to the Baali, and in most older sources it is said that they whorship Satan, but Lore of the Clans claims for some reason they they serve God by &quot;the necessary evil&quot; and <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Lasombra#Angellis_Ater\" target=\"_blank\">the White Wolf wiki claims for some reason that they were &quot;anti-Infernalists&quot;</a> (without giving any source).<br /> <br /> So what are these guys what Path or Road are they following?<ul><li>&quot;Hard Core Infernalits&quot; meaning <b>Path of Evil Revelations</b> (modern)/<b>Path of Screams</b> (Dark Age)</li> <li>&quot;Doing the necessary evil&quot; meaning <b>Path of Nigh</b> (modern)/ <b>Road of Night</b> (Dark Age)</li> <li>&quot;Nice Satanists&quot; meaning <b>Via Adversarius</b> (Dark Age, I don't think there is a modern equivalent)</li> <li>or since there is also something mentioned about them being addicted to Obtenebration maybe some thing like the <b>Road of the Abyss</b> (Dark Age)</li> <li>or something completely different?</li> </ul><br /> And do you think the bloodline would practice Abyss Mysticism or Dark Thaumaturgy?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T12:45:08-08:00","id":1531135,"title":"","content":"The contradictions are likely because World of Darkness writers sometimes ignore continuity when creating new material. Sometimes this is done because they may not have clearly understood what an earlier writer meant, sometimes it may be because they did not bother to reread passages and inadvertently create a contradiction they did not intend, and sometimes because they intentionally mean to change continuity because of a dislike of earlier material or because they think their own ideas are better. This is one reason I say now there are in fact multiple &quot;continuities&quot; out there with their own canon, and that the differences between these competing canons is similar to the old Earth-One, Earth-Two, etc. of DC Comics which used the same concepts in different ways.<br /> <br /> I believe the Angellis Ater were first introduced in Libellus Sanguinus I in which they are clearly Satanists using a mockery of Catholic sacraments. They believe the darkness they summon from Obtenebration comes from hell and are loyal to their demonic overlords. These vampires are clearly infernalists. What Path would they use? Well, that depends. According to the original Sabbat guides the original Path of Evil Revelations was created by a mortal group of infernalists embraced by a Sabbat Brujah anti-tribu centuries after the Middle Ages. So that Path could not have actually existed in the Dark Ages setting, except of course that it does (Via Diabolis). The writers for Vampire: the Dark Ages would create a lot of their own continuity to meet the needs of the new setting and clearly had no problem contradicting the original canon. If you want to reconcile the two, we could say that both groups independently created similar Paths which we treat as mechanically same/similar for convenience.<br /> <br /> In Clanbook: Baali, the Angellis Ater are mentioned again. The Angellis Ater are not Baali, but allies to the Baali. But as a result of their interaction some Baali (Azaneal and his childer/followers) have learned Obtenebration. But as written, the Azaneali are NOT members of the Angellis Ater. They are just allied to them and have learned Obtenebration as a result. However, because of their connection some people may have confused the two and treated them as the same sect/cult.<br /> <br /> I have not read Lore of the Clans, but if it is treating the Angellis Ater as &quot;serving God&quot; in any fashion, they have clearly changed canon. Perhaps because the writer wanted to combine several different strains of Lasombra together, likely wanting to tie in the Path of Night with the Angellis Ater. But the Path of Night was first introduced in the Revised corebook and was mentioned to be followed mostly by young Lasombra, implying this is a relatively new Path. In its path history section, the Angellis Ater are mentioned as possibly be involved in its creation and dissemination. However, if so then the Angellis Ater would not be followers of the Path of Night themselves. Instead, they were involved in its creation in order to corrupt other Lasombra into doing evil under the mistaken idea they were doing the work of God (and perhaps recruit new Lasombra into their infernalist cult). Another possibility is that the Angellis Ater did not survive, but the creators of the Path of Night knew something about them and incorporated some of their ideas into the new Path. Lore of the Clans seems to have either not understood this distinction, ignored it, or decided to tweak it by combining them together and retroactively changing the Angellis Ater as a result.<br /> <br /> In any case, I would personally use some version of the Path of Evil Revelations / Via Diabolis for their Path. Having said that, it is entirely possible there are Lasombra following the Path of Night who nevertheless call themselves the Angellis Ater because they wrongly believe this is what those Lasombra believed, are doing it to troll people, or who believe they developed out of them and are appropriating the name to create a false linkage between the two groups. In these kinds of small occult groups, political disagreements, splits, and offshoots all claiming to be the one &quot;true&quot; group is not uncommon.<br /> <br /> I would also use Abyss Mysticism instead of Dark Thaumaturgy because 1) their original interest of the darkness of Obtenebration is what lead them into their infernalist worship, and 2) using it would help distinguish them from other infernalists who would use Dark Thaumaturgy instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T12:47:12-08:00","id":1531136,"title":"","content":"Given that in V20 the Bloodline is a merger between two different things and there is so little lore around them, there are good points to be made for any of the options you listed. Azaneal was definitely on the Nergali side of the Baali and the Order of Moloch directly opposed him, which would put the Angellis Ater in the infernalist camp rather than the quasi anti-infernalist camp of the Molochim. I probably would make the decision for Road and type of Blood Sorcery dependent on the specific character rather than the Bloodline as a whole, especially because there are so few of them.<br /> <br /> The tricky thing is, they have different characteristics depending from which side of the two Clans you approach them. When you come at them from the Lasombra side, they are Road of Night / Abyss Mystic type of characters. From the Baali side, you're looking at Path of Screams / Dark Thauma. I personally think the former would be more suited for a PC and the latter more for an antagonist NPC. Although to be completely honest, I'm biased there because I think approaching the Children with Obtenebration is the more interesting option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T13:25:04-08:00","id":1531139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531130-v20-and-earlied-angellis-ater-what-path-road?p=1531136#post1531136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I personally think the former would be more suited for a PC and the latter more for an antagonist NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I my case it is more a theoretical question than something I actually want to use in a game.<br /> <br /> Abyss Mystic has of cause if you actually want to use them the benefit that it seems to me the more usefull of the two, Dark Thaumaturgy seems also to have been changed a lot between edition and has when it comes to what the paths do also some redundacy with Daimonion (which the Angellis Ater allready have).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-20T12:58:15-08:00","id":1531209,"title":"","content":"By looking a bit through the books, does anybody now what edition had rules (meaning Bloodline Disciplines and Weakness) for the Angellis Ater and in what book (any maybe even on what page) I can find them?<br /> Sofar the only I could find were the ones in the V20 corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T11:22:12-08:00","id":1531298,"title":"","content":"<i>Libellus Sanguinis 1</i> describes the original Angellis Ater (p.22) but doesn't stat them differently from other Lasombra. <i>Clanbook: Baali </i>has a box on Azaneali and their connection with the Angellis Ater (p.36) and offers to swap either Daimonion or Presence with Obtenebration. Their Clan Flaw doesn't change, though.<br /> As far as I'm aware only V20 presents the 'unified' bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T23:49:53-08:00","id":1531599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531130-v20-and-earlied-angellis-ater-what-path-road?p=1531298#post1531298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Clanbook: Baali </i>has a box on Azaneali and their connection with the Angellis Ater (p.36) and offers to swap either Daimonion or Presence with Obtenebration. Their Clan Flaw doesn't change, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>But those are Azaneali (meaning Baali) and not Angellis Ater (meaning Lasombra).<br /> <br /> So the Angellis Ater never had stats before V20?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T12:47:10-08:00","id":1531737,"title":"","content":"At least none that I know of. If somebody knows a source that contradicts this let me know, but I think prior to V20 the Angellis Ater were just a faction within the Lasombra, not a bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T14:27:53-08:00","id":1531744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531130-v20-and-earlied-angellis-ater-what-path-road?p=1531737#post1531737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least none that I know of. If somebody knows a source that contradicts this let me know, but I think prior to V20 the Angellis Ater were just a faction within the Lasombra, not a bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I imagine the intent with the original interpretation from <i>Liber Sanguinis I</i> was that Angellis Ater vampires were just Lasombra who learned Dark Thaumaturgy out-of-Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-29T20:42:05-08:00","id":1531766,"title":"","content":"My own headcanon is that Azaneal was originally a Lasombra, and member of the Angellis Ater, who underwent the Baali rites and was re-Embraced as a Baali. He brought a number of members of the Angellis Ater along with him, most of whom were also re-Embraced as Baali, enough that the Azaneali became a major Baali bloodline. The Angellis Ater still have close ties to the Azaneali and there's a lot of back and forth between both groups. The Azaneali recruit from the Angellis Ater when they can, and the Angellis Ater use the Azaneali's links to demons as a source to learn Dark Thaumaturgy. Outsiders often don't see much of a difference between the two groups.<br /> <br /> Some Angellis Ater have sworn full pacts with demons, but most of them view themselves as demons and have little desire to become someone's slaves. So they tend to think of the deals they make with devils as pacts made between equals, but a number of them have ended up in over their heads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T05:40:19-08:00","id":1531778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531130-v20-and-earlied-angellis-ater-what-path-road#post1531130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused by the Angellis Ater and what actually their deal is since the different sources are pretty contradictory.<br /> <br /> And do you think the bloodline would practice Abyss Mysticism or Dark Thaumaturgy?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Consider who the Angellis Ater are, they are in a unique position of having access to both Abyss Mysticism and Dark Thaumaturgy. I guess it depends on the particular Vampiress or Vampire. Various Unlife choices and decisions might place her or him among circles and groups that can give tutelage and advancement In these Disciplines and Powers. I would say that by default Abyss Mysticism is probably the preferred choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}